In19, the role of mitochondrial inner membrane protein (IMMT) as a molecular biomarker in breast cancer was analyzed using The Cancer GenomeAtlas (TCGA) and clinical samples. Their results confirmed that IMMT expression was highly overexpressed in breast cancer tissue relative to normal tissue. In their work, they discovered IMMT to be an independent prognosis factor that positively correlates with clinical factors like tumor size (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
