The proposed diagnostic architecture illustrated in Fig. 3 a complete hybrid model that merges and syncs the spatial mapping ability of 1D Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) with the sequential dependency modelling capability of Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory Networks (BiLSTMs) for in-depth analysis of the 236 Gene Signature will be created45. After being processed through the two parallel branches of the ranked genomic input, the local motifs detected within the CNN layer post flattening and the global contexts discovered within the BiLSTM layer will be integrated via the concatenation operation in the layer as outlined above. : \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
